[
  {
    "sha": "eae2d557a81bc80a042abbb7f0db8ea845a16a21",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGVhZTJkNTU3YTgxYmM4MGEwNDJhYmJiN2YwZGI4ZWE4NDVhMTZhMjE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T20:26:44Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T20:26:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): G43.4 posts write the joint angles of the tilt chain\n\nThe Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts wrote the stream's pose letters (axis =\nRy(B)·Rx(A)·Z) as the A and B words. On the tilt head the A rotary\ncarries the B rotary, so the machine reads those words as\nRx(A)·Ry(B)·Z: a different tool axis when A and B both turn.\n\nA prelude function, chainAngles, now solves the joint angles for the\nnest order of the machine file, and the machine check judges the same\nangles through machine::tilt_chain::joint_angles. A chain whose nest is\nunstated, a pair rotary stated along -X or -Y, and a C turn on an\nA-outer chain are refused by name.\n\nFixes #4417\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
